config BCM2835_FB
	bool "BCM2835/2710 VideoCore-firmware framebuffer (HDMI)"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_BRCM_BCM2835_FB_ENABLED
	select RASPBERRYPI_FIRMWARE
	help
	  Enable the VideoCore-firmware-backed HDMI framebuffer driver
	  for the BCM2835 / BCM2710 family. Requests a framebuffer from
	  the VC GPU via the property-tag mailbox interface and exposes
	  it through the Zephyr display driver API. Pixel format is
	  selectable per-instance via the `pixel-format` DT property --
	  PIXEL_FORMAT_ARGB_8888 (default) or PIXEL_FORMAT_RGB_565.

	  The HDMI scanout itself is brought up by the VideoCore boot
	  firmware according to config.txt; without `hdmi_force_hotplug=1`
	  the GPU only enables HDMI when a monitor is connected at power-on.
